{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition","id":777632,"title":"what this humble changeling fan wishes for the C20 edition.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-01T02:12:44-08:00","id":777632,"title":"what this humble changeling fan wishes for the C20 edition.","content":"Long time fan of the changeling game line, but awesome thought it was, there were a few things i wish had been done better. consider this a wish list from me, a fan. maybe the developers can find something useful.<br /> <br /> -Less cutesy art: while the wonder of dreams was is a big part of the setting, the artwork often times seemed to cutesy, even childish to really fit in as a WoD title. changeling has the potential to be the darkest of the main titles after all, whats more terrifying then the nightmares of a child? it doesnt all have to be grim and dark, but some grittier artwork to help balance the lighter toned stuff would be nice.<br /> <br /> - Streamlined and simplified systems for glamour and banality: this is a major gripe i had with previous editions. to many refrences to ability scores and a confusing series of dice rolls.<br /> <br /> - clearer descriptions of the difference between chimerical and banal reality.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6111-thecosmicgoose","name":"thecosmicgoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T08:34:58-08:00","id":777776,"title":"","content":"On the subject of gaining Glamour, I'd like to see it be made more realistically doable. This may come in as part of making Changelings more magically impressive, but as it was, they could expend their entire store in a single scene or less, and then spend many many sessions unable to take the scenes necessary to Ravage, let alone the enormous amount of time needed for Reverie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:00:29-08:00","id":778147,"title":"","content":"Ravaging should also be more of a grey area, morally, than outright black. The LARP rules, as I understand it, were more forgiving, meaning you could Ravage someone without breaking them for good.<br /> <br /> If, rather than destroying someone's capacity to dream, Ravaging simply inspires them with dark and savage passions (with the knock-on effects such passions have on the outside world, as the Ravaged human goes and slakes dark thirsts), then it would make that particular method of gaining Glamour more appealing, give the Unseelie more nuance than just 'bad guys', and create a narrative tool that Storytellers can use to make characters deal with the consequences of their actions. <br /> <br /> My feeling has always been that rather than capping power by making resources artificially scarce and having very high difficulties, it's more in-keeping with the themes and mood of the oWoD to balance power with responsibility. Yes, you can suck Glamour out of nearby humans, but the effect is that they become temporary vortices of pain and darkness, or else magnets for Banality, and this has repercussions. Yes, you can cast your cantrips, but it draws chimera closer, and not all of them play nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-03-2015, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T10:12:41-08:00","id":778429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thecosmicgoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition#post777632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Less cutesy art: while the wonder of dreams was is a big part of the setting, the artwork often times seemed to cutesy, even childish to really fit in as a WoD title. changeling has the potential to be the darkest of the main titles after all, whats more terrifying then the nightmares of a child? it doesnt all have to be grim and dark, but some grittier artwork to help balance the lighter toned stuff would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a new kith called the Teddy Bear. It's based on a certain series of illustrations in 2E. The dev team thinks it'll be super popular since it seems to always get brought up in any Changeling discussion. It'll have an exclusive balloon based art, plus one of it's birthrights can immediately banish any form of darkness for a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T19:38:21-08:00","id":778763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=778429#post778429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a new kith called the Teddy Bear. It's based on a certain series of illustrations in 2E. The dev team thinks it'll be super popular since it seems to always get brought up in any Changeling discussion. It'll have an exclusive balloon based art, plus one of it's birthrights can immediately banish any form of darkness for a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> are we talking physical or metaphorical darkness here? because if its physical than suddenly the lasombra are in deep trouble. I can just imagine the PRICELESS look on an ancient vampire's face when he gets his ass soundly handed too him by a stuffed animal...suddenly i wish it wasn't a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T21:05:29-08:00","id":778791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=778147#post778147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravaging should also be more of a grey area, morally, than outright black. The LARP rules, as I understand it, were more forgiving, meaning you could Ravage someone without breaking them for good.<br /> <br /> If, rather than destroying someone's capacity to dream, Ravaging simply inspires them with dark and savage passions (with the knock-on effects such passions have on the outside world, as the Ravaged human goes and slakes dark thirsts), then it would make that particular method of gaining Glamour more appealing, give the Unseelie more nuance than just 'bad guys', and create a narrative tool that Storytellers can use to make characters deal with the consequences of their actions.<br /> <br /> My feeling has always been that rather than capping power by making resources artificially scarce and having very high difficulties, it's more in-keeping with the themes and mood of the oWoD to balance power with responsibility. Yes, you can suck Glamour out of nearby humans, but the effect is that they become temporary vortexes of pain and darkness, or else magnets for Banality, and this has repercussions. Yes, you can cast your cantrips, but it draws chimera closer, and not all of them play nice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's one of the RARE things I thought the Larp did better with Ravaging Thresholds. I could go out and inspire ANGER this could be pure on being an asshole but also get people to rise up and rage against their circumstances. An Unseelie feeding and inspiring Political activism against the shit the world has handed people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T01:39:39-08:00","id":778860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=778791#post778791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's one of the RARE things I thought the Larp did better with Ravaging Thresholds. I could go out and inspire ANGER this could be pure on being an asshole but also get people to rise up and rage against their circumstances. An Unseelie feeding and inspiring Political activism against the shit the world has handed people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's great. CTL also does something similar. It ties in better with the 'Glamour is Free' thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T07:08:35-08:00","id":778983,"title":"","content":"I think people are confusing Ravaging and Rhapsody. Ravaging, in the rules in the C:tD core book that I own, just makes people feel enervated and out of capacity to be imaginative. They're &quot;emotioned out,&quot; so to speak. They'll recover after some rest and maybe some healthier mental activities (as Ravaging is pretty explicitly feeding on &quot;mental junk food&quot; and less-than-healthy emotional encouragement; euphoria for less than solid reason, anger and pain and lust and fervor for their own sakes, ginned up and concentrated and then wrung out...and even that's not always BAD, just exhausting and without leaving behind a sense of accomplishment, which is its main difference from Reverie).<br /> <br /> Rhapsody burns out the victim completely, inspiring all of their current and consuming their future creative potential to enormous heights (but, perhaps, not as much overall as might have come from a steady series of Reveries) to make one magnificent work, a magnum opus that literally will never be topped or equaled because the creator will never create again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T15:53:22-08:00","id":779338,"title":"","content":"One thing on Ravaging? How can a Ailil Childling safely feed without accumulating LOTS of banality swiftly... <br /> <br /> Also I'd prefer for inspiring terror or dread, to not make someone banal neccessarily<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T16:50:55-08:00","id":779360,"title":"","content":"My main desire for C20 is to feature a wider range of perspectives. The earlier editions seem to have been written primarily from a Seelie Childling's perspective, which results in Unseelie coming off as baddies and Grumps feeling like they have one foot in the grave. It would be bad enough if it was just fluff that carried these biases; but far too often, you found them in the mechanics: Unseelie Legacies were written as the sort of thing villains would have, and the Grump's balance of Glamour vs. Banality <i>did</i> put him on the verge of falling to the latter, without any compensation. <br /> <br /> I could see addressing the former issue by remaking the Legacies to feel more like an Order vs. Freedom sort of thing, by including some Seelie Legacies that feel oppressive rather than heroic and some Unseelie Legacies that feel liberated rather than abusive. Better, present two sides (good and bad) to <i>every</i> Legacy, whether it be Seelie or Unseelie. <br /> <br /> The latter could be addressed by playing up the dangers of too much Glamour, and the role of Banality in maintaining one's sanity: balance changelings on a ledge between losing the ability to imagine and dream on the one hand and losing touch with the real world on the other. Or not, as that effectively puts the Wilders in a preferential role\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T21:04:55-08:00","id":779523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=778983#post778983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people are confusing Ravaging and Rhapsody. Ravaging, in the rules in the C:tD core book that I own, just makes people feel enervated and out of capacity to be imaginative. They're &quot;emotioned out,&quot; so to speak. They'll recover after some rest and maybe some healthier mental activities (as Ravaging is pretty explicitly feeding on &quot;mental junk food&quot; and less-than-healthy emotional encouragement; euphoria for less than solid reason, anger and pain and lust and fervor for their own sakes, ginned up and concentrated and then wrung out...and even that's not always BAD, just exhausting and without leaving behind a sense of accomplishment, which is its main difference from Reverie).<br /> <br /> Rhapsody burns out the victim completely, inspiring all of their current and consuming their future creative potential to enormous heights (but, perhaps, not as much overall as might have come from a steady series of Reveries) to make one magnificent work, a magnum opus that literally will never be topped or equaled because the creator will never create again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But its constantly hit out there that Ravaging causes them to dream less in the future that do it enough you kill their dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T22:06:24-08:00","id":779544,"title":"","content":"I never quite got that impression, but I'll take your word for it. It's been ages since I read the core book. (Which is the only one I own.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:30:24-08:00","id":779659,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the 'killing dreams' thing crops up again and again. Rhapsody, of course, is even more extreme.<br /> <br /> Legacies, I agree, also need to be cleaned up. They're just completely two dimensional as written. I usually dropped them for Natures and Demeanors anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:17:47-08:00","id":779825,"title":"","content":"I think I've said it elsewhere, but I'll repeat it here: I'd also like to see Banality be not &quot;purely bad.&quot; There is some lip service given to the notion that Changelings need to balance their two sides, to hold to the mortal as well as the mystical, lest they be lost to one or the other. But actually being lost to the Dreaming is VERY HARD as written, taking almost deliberate effort, and doesn't really have any sense that accepting banality will help counterbalance it. Banality is just bad.<br /> <br /> I think it would be more interesting if Banality and Glamour were both resources, and having too much of either made it harder to interact sanely/rationally with the other world. That there is power in allowing the mundane reality to supercede the Dreaming, but that one can ALSO do the reverse.<br /> <br /> One thing I think would make Glamour more useful would be if Echoes weren't a flaw, but were instead a thing one could develop and cultivate as one grew stronger in Glamour's permanent rating. Adhering to one's Echoes - the fae superstitions/restrictions/requirements - earns bits of Glamour. So ignoring somebody whose clothing is inside-out or refusing to even try to use magic on them would potentially earn you Glamour for being properly Fae. The trouble would be that, without sufficient Banlity, one wouldn't be ABLE to CHOOSE to ignore it. This would both make it less likely to give temporary glamour AND make you more restricted. (Though probably some base level of glamour should be higher for even BEING in that position.)<br /> <br /> Make the madness rewarding, and make ignoring it rewarding, but make either a bit contradictory to the other so that it's a choice. More power either way can be had by leaning more the proper direction, but it becomes harder to interact with or resist or what-have-you the other side of things, and increasingly hard to &quot;recover&quot; the balance point before one is lost, one way or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:41:52-08:00","id":780059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=779360#post779360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main desire for C20 is to feature a wider range of perspectives. The earlier editions seem to have been written primarily from a Seelie Childling's perspective, which results in Unseelie coming off as baddies and Grumps feeling like they have one foot in the grave. It would be bad enough if it was just fluff that carried these biases; but far too often, you found them in the mechanics: Unseelie Legacies were written as the sort of thing villains would have, and the Grump's balance of Glamour vs. Banality <i>did</i> put him on the verge of falling to the latter, without any compensation.<br /> <br /> I could see addressing the former issue by remaking the Legacies to feel more like an Order vs. Freedom sort of thing, by including some Seelie Legacies that feel oppressive rather than heroic and some Unseelie Legacies that feel liberated rather than abusive. Better, present two sides (good and bad) to <i>every</i> Legacy, whether it be Seelie or Unseelie.<br /> <br /> The latter could be addressed by playing up the dangers of too much Glamour, and the role of Banality in maintaining one's sanity: balance changelings on a ledge between losing the ability to imagine and dream on the one hand and losing touch with the real world on the other. Or not, as that effectively puts the Wilders in a preferential role\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a big fan of order vs Freedom vs Order. I'd be ok with Straight Heroes vs Monsters because we've had decades of ways to show how to be a good Monster and a ways to be a evil Hero. Or Unseelie are creepy and Dark Seelie are pretty and Light these are not the same as Good and Evil though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T04:16:12-08:00","id":780492,"title":"","content":"Well, as somebody who would love to get into Changeling but is put off by the idea that science=bad (which I understand some writers were lighter on, but it still annoys me) and being confused as to what banality is supposed to be have left me putting it off for the moment.<br /> <br /> The problem is I love the idea of Changeling, I just find it insulting. So my main desire for C20 is to see science embraced as something that can be genuinely wonderful and even creative, and a tightening of what banality is. I think Banality should be the lack of wonder, he acceptance of what is without struggling to find out why, knowing your toaster makes toast without being interested in who is does so reliably, seeing a painting as just a picture and not a carefully put together piece of colour and shape. Then make Banality able to deny Chimerical reality, properly, as in a place infused with Banality inflicts chimerical damage if you aren't sufficiently Banal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T07:44:32-08:00","id":780552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=780492#post780492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my main desire for C20 is to see science embraced as something that can be genuinely wonderful and even creative, and a tightening of what banality is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say odds are good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T09:59:18-08:00","id":780596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=780552#post780552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say odds are good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I'm just worried because Changeling could supplant Demon as my favourite cWoD game, but only if it's done right and realises that several of my friends are so happy and creative because they are scientists. That reminds me, I do also want a Glamour economy closer to Demon's Faith economy, I'm a goddam fairy, I should at least be able to be terrifying a few times a day, or to give humans gifts that just plain don't make sense, not be trying to grab a few crumbs of power to make people happy. Even just waking up with a handful of glamour points a day would be far better than fighting tooth and nail for the,.<br /> <br /> On the gifts front, an example of what fairies would traditionally give people they liked, such as a liver that is a brick made our of bees, much more interesting than your old liver. Ideally just a list of random items you can roll on as many times as you want to freak players out, especially when their lord gives them a brick that looks like a brick made out of bricks, it'll drive them insane looking for the thing that makes it weird/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T13:35:50-08:00","id":780686,"title":"","content":"Well, as a changeling fan one thing I don't want it to change is the glamour economy. Because as whitewolf wiki suggested, glamour is a diamond form of all others. It should be challenging.<br /> <br /> The other thing is that, I think banality is well defined. Banality it self is also an energy like glamour. One of the book says that some changeling try to use this &quot;scientific glamour&quot; but they become dautian. Think two circle, one is inside of another. First area is &quot;consensus&quot; and other big area is enchanted world. As a changeling what you do is dream and add new stuff to bigger area. If you want to take it into &quot;wyrd&quot;, you should take it into barrier (mists, also the second circle). Banality is opposite force that try to stop you, and glamour is the energy that make it easier, or emitted by this process (musing). Scientist can be creative, but they are closed to myth. If they are okey with myth, and believe that it can be real. Well, they are not so banal then. Problem is that what is your banality for. If you are denying them you are banal in changeling eyes, not for technocracy.<br /> <br /> The biggest mistake in all changeling books and setting is that they are hyper banal. They always use same border type in all books. Setting has same character sheet as others. Be different, be wyld! For example, make the sheet looks like snail. Why not? It is creative.<br /> <br /> Also please stop using hazy character arts. Please show them in mundane way so that people stop misunderstand them. I don't want sluagh as in core book, white page and golden borders. Make them worthy of being scary! They are embodied shape of horror tales.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I have two suggestion. First of all, please bring ritual system. I will give an example at the end. Secondly, please bring &quot;feature&quot; property of dark age fae. We need to customize our kiths, other ways they are so banal that I don't want to play same kith at third time. I want to customize them.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> My example for a ritual, (This is belong to one of my players)<br /> <br /> An eshu named Ishtar has a treasure named as &quot;Sher-Name(Book of Nightmares)&quot;. This book holds nightmare chimeras that Ishtar extracted from its enemies or friends.<br /> In darkness, Ishtar uses his &quot;Soothsay 1 Omen&quot; to understand his opponents most terrifying fear. He uses a certain bunk. This bunk should be a sentence that contains &quot;Nightmare,Fear and Darkness&quot;. However, he cannot use this sentence again in his life!.<br /> <br /> After understanding the fear, he starts to create this as a thought in opponents mind. He uses talecraft art for this. He starts to describe it, and chimera starts to emerge. (Opponent rolls willpower to resist it and subtracts success from talecraft cantrip). This cause opponent to think and describe what is emerging.<br /> <br /> In third phase, after chimera described as whole, it emerges from the opponents dreams to dreaming. It starts to attack opponent. It should not have to be physical attack, but can be mental one. In this phase the storyteller(I mean eshu) selects an obvious and ridiculous flaw to this creature (for example giant crocodile tickles). Also, if opponent is a really good dreamer and believer he/she can be add a flaw to chimera (for example sleeping in front of bear can be effective). (talecraft art will be used in this phase also).<br /> <br /> In fourth phase, chimera goes to &quot;Sher-Name&quot; and become a page. And can be summoned as treasure power later.(But only once).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T14:38:53-08:00","id":780716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=780686#post780686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as a changeling fan one thing I don't want it to change is the glamour economy. Because as whitewolf wiki suggested, glamour is a diamond form of all others. It should be challenging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings are creatures of one part mundanity and one part magic. They should have the ability for it to be something they can do, not something they should horde just in case. Maybe it's 'regain one Glamour per scene', maybe it's 'regain one Glamour for a full night's sleep'. At the very least, Changelings should be able to regain Glamour from their own dreams without writing a novel or creating a painting (I'd like to point out that artist Changelings can theoretically use Rapture every few days, an actor takes at least a week, possibly several, and an author requires at least a month, probably two or three to reach rapture, not counting editing). My solution would be to allow a Glamour roll (difficulty 7) every day a Changeling works on their pet project(s), to gain small rewards and the ability to cast more than five Cantrips a campaign (an exaggeration, but boy regaining Glamour is slow). I use Demon's faith economy as a benchmark as it's as stable as Vampire's is while being smaller, with beginning Demons having a trickle of 0-3 Faith a day and an occasional boost from Rapture, although I have no desire to have it be that high. Just reliable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other thing is that, I think banality is well defined. Banality it self is also an energy like glamour. One of the book says that some changeling try to use this &quot;scientific glamour&quot; but they become dautian. Think two circle, one is inside of another. First area is &quot;consensus&quot; and other big area is enchanted world. As a changeling what you do is dream and add new stuff to bigger area. If you want to take it into &quot;wyrd&quot;, you should take it into barrier (mists, also the second circle). Banality is opposite force that try to stop you, and glamour is the energy that make it easier, or emitted by this process (musing). Scientist can be creative, but they are closed to myth. If they are okey with myth, and believe that it can be real. Well, they are not so banal then. Problem is that what is your banality for. If you are denying them you are banal in changeling eyes, not for technocracy. </div> </div> </div>Have you ever met a Scientist? They are the exact opposite of banal. They can be so fascinated with stuff that they'll stop GMing for 20 minutes to tell you why the yellow LEDs are better for lighting their boat than traditional lightbulbs. They dream, and dream big, and add more to their area. An artist might think 'this thing here would to cool to have', while a scientist would look at it and say 'you know what would be cool? If we got a couple of chemists and engineers, and made this reality', followed later by 'well, okay, maybe we shouldn't give everybody jetpacks'. Was it artists who built the world's first hoverbike?<br /> <br /> Now let me try a simple thought experiment. I want wonder, and have two books to pick from, 'Assorted Egyptian Myths' and 'How to Teach Quantum Physics to Your Dog'. Which would you pick? I would pick the second one, as would over half my friends, because science is cool and oh look there's this area of it that I never understood and can I have a particle accelerator Mr University Man please?<br /> <br /> Yes, a scientist's first thought at meeting an angel is 'what happens if I take it apart', but that's because if we can put it back together again, we can then build more angels! Imagine if you could create angels to solve all the world's problems!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The biggest mistake in all changeling books and setting is that they are hyper banal. They always use same border type in all books. Setting has same character sheet as others. Be different, be wyld! For example, make the sheet looks like snail. Why not? It is creative. </div> </div> </div>Oh boy, this is an art issue, and the art is in my opinion fine, Changeling is more about the horror underlying the hope, sort of like a reverse Wraith.<br /> <br /> Plus that character sheet would be a pain to use. I can say that the current character sheet is functional, so why change it? I've played with more confusing sheets, sometimes simplicity and standardisation is good. Plus it means if I do want to run a crossover chronicle, I don't have one character sheet of a vastly different style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also please stop using hazy character arts. Please show them in mundane way so that people stop misunderstand them. I don't want sluagh as in core book, white page and golden borders. Make them worthy of being scary! They are embodied shape of horror tales. </div> </div> </div>It could be worse, Hunter the Reckoning could have pictures of a Hunter fighting off multiple Garou without any trouble.<br /> <br /> More variation is good, but I'd prefer quality writing and pictures before more variation in art.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, I have two suggestion. First of all, please bring ritual system. I will give an example at the end. Secondly, please bring &quot;feature&quot; property of dark age fae. We need to customize our kiths, other ways they are so banal that I don't want to play same kith at third time. I want to customize them. </div> </div> </div>I don't really see a need for a ritual system, beyond 'getting the knowledge and stuff for big stuff might take a subplot. Also, while I agree more customisation of kiths would be good, I'm not against the C20 corebook just presenting 'standard' versions and leaving customisation for a 'player's guide' or 'companion'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T02:32:14-08:00","id":781039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=780716#post780716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 'you know what would be cool? If we got a couple of chemists and engineers, and made this reality'</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, It seems that I couldn't made the point. This phrase is the best example word of a banal person, I mean in world of darkness. I my self is an engineer, and I think I am a whole of banal sh*t, but why?.<br /> <br /> Well, this phrase is banal because it actually exist. You do not need to bring it into reality, it exist in reality. Imagination do not come from you, but come through dreaming. The concept of a car can be found in dreaming, but not in a standard way. People limited the reality by making up rules. This rules are the foundation of banality. They push away other probabilities. You do not need engineers to made it real, you can use some &quot;GOK&quot; to make a machine better. You can just fix a machine by kicking it. These are the other possibilities, but a engineer comes and says &quot;you cannot fix by just kicking it. It should be a coincidence.&quot;. This is the banality. The Engineer just killed its glare, made it mundane.<br /> <br /> Nockers can be counted as scientist, but they are not banal. The problem is not the science, its approach just like religion. It only want to explain situations on its reality, and deny or approach in same manner for &quot;miracles or myth&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T04:04:16-08:00","id":781065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=781039#post781039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, It seems that I couldn't made the point. This phrase is the best example word of a banal person, I mean in world of darkness. I my self is an engineer, and I think I am a whole of banal sh*t, but why?.<br /> <br /> Well, this phrase is banal because it actually exist. You do not need to bring it into reality, it exist in reality. Imagination do not come from you, but come through dreaming. The concept of a car can be found in dreaming, but not in a standard way. People limited the reality by making up rules. This rules are the foundation of banality. They push away other probabilities. You do not need engineers to made it real, you can use some &amp;quot;GOK&amp;quot; to make a machine better. You can just fix a machine by kicking it. These are the other possibilities, but a engineer comes and says &amp;quot;you cannot fix by just kicking it. It should be a coincidence.&amp;quot;. This is the banality. The Engineer just killed its glare, made it mundane.<br /> <br /> Nockers can be counted as scientist, but they are not banal. The problem is not the science, its approach just like religion. It only want to explain situations on its reality, and deny or approach in same manner for &amp;quot;miracles or myth&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the dogma of science is what is limiting, just as the dogma of religion is. True Glamour arises from possibility, rather than limitations. Science isn't banal because it creates or imagines; it's banal because it insists in its own way of doing things to the exclusion of others.<br /> <br /> Scientists can still be creative and science can still generate Glamour, but that tension between its tendency to limit and its tendency to generate is part of the fraught reality of Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T05:27:20-08:00","id":781078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=781039#post781039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, It seems that I couldn't made the point. This phrase is the best example word of a banal person, I mean in world of darkness. I my self is an engineer, and I think I am a whole of banal sh*t, but why?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? So if I said 'jetpacks are cool, why don't I try to make a jetpack' I'd be banal?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, this phrase is banal because it actually exist. You do not need to bring it into reality, it exist in reality. Imagination do not come from you, but come through dreaming. The concept of a car can be found in dreaming, but not in a standard way. People limited the reality by making up rules. This rules are the foundation of banality. They push away other probabilities. You do not need engineers to made it real, you can use some &quot;GOK&quot; to make a machine better. You can just fix a machine by kicking it. These are the other possibilities, but a engineer comes and says &quot;you cannot fix by just kicking it. It should be a coincidence.&quot;. This is the banality. The Engineer just killed its glare, made it mundane. </div> </div> </div>So by making something that didn't exist before, I'm banal? Well I suppose cities, swords, clothing, literature, art (because the physical painting had to push away possibilities to be able to exist), language, and basically everything that defines both mortal and fairy culture is inherently banal, because they had to have rules applied to the idea in order to make them reality. Total amount of glamour you can harvest from anything human=0.<br /> <br /> Maybe when I make my jetpack I push away some possibilities of what a jetpack could be. Maybe instead of a propeller it's a jet engine strapped to my back. Then somebody else comes along, sees my jetpack, and says 'you know what would be awesome? If that worked by electromagnetism', and then they go away and start trying to build it. Then somebody else comes along and says 'that's cool, but you know what would be cooler? A rocket bike', and then they go away and build it. Then somebody sees the rocket pike, and decides to add it into their general purpose robot. Then their robot's AI becomes sapient and goes off to paint a picture of a suit of powered armour, somebody sees the painting and tries to build it. Dreams becoming reality inspiring dreams.<br /> <br /> That not be how you see science, but that's how science is meant to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nockers can be counted as scientist, but they are not banal. The problem is not the science, its approach just like religion. It only want to explain situations on its reality, and deny or approach in same manner for &quot;miracles or myth&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem is how science is treated. Without the scientific method no science could get done, so you sacrifice one possibility for another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T07:51:15-08:00","id":781135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=781078#post781078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh? So if I said 'jetpacks are cool, why don't I try to make a jetpack' I'd be banal?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So by making something that didn't exist before, I'm banal? Well I suppose cities, swords, clothing, literature, art (because the physical painting had to push away possibilities to be able to exist), language, and basically everything that defines both mortal and fairy culture is inherently banal, because they had to have rules applied to the idea in order to make them reality. Total amount of glamour you can harvest from anything human=0.<br /> <br /> Maybe when I make my jetpack I push away some possibilities of what a jetpack could be. Maybe instead of a propeller it's a jet engine strapped to my back. Then somebody else comes along, sees my jetpack, and says 'you know what would be awesome? If that worked by electromagnetism', and then they go away and start trying to build it. Then somebody else comes along and says 'that's cool, but you know what would be cooler? A rocket bike', and then they go away and build it. Then somebody sees the rocket pike, and decides to add it into their general purpose robot. Then their robot's AI becomes sapient and goes off to paint a picture of a suit of powered armour, somebody sees the painting and tries to build it. Dreams becoming reality inspiring dreams.<br /> <br /> That not be how you see science, but that's how science is meant to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Part of the problem is how science is treated. Without the scientific method no science could get done, so you sacrifice one possibility for another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making things isn't banal. Discovering things isn't banal. But there's a tension in *proving* something, as, in essence, you're eliminating the possibility of those things that are disproved. Magick means all things are possible; science means only some things are possible, and only by the rules of science (reason, progress, etc). <br /> <br /> Science can still create, which is great, but it limits things and rules possibilities out by definition. A new eureka can generate Glamour, but the plodding, repetitive methodology that gets there is often, ironically, very, very banal. That isn't a flaw in the setting--that's it's strength. The human and the fae, the Dreaming and the banal, the free and the organised are all things that need to exist. Imbalance is the real problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T08:03:15-08:00","id":781140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=781135#post781135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making things isn't banal. Discovering things isn't banal. But there's a tension in *proving* something, as, in essence, you're eliminating the possibility of those things that are disproved. Magick means all things are possible; science means only some things are possible, and only by the rules of science (reason, progress, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me put it this way, I hate the idea of science being banal. I agree that the scientific method itself can be banal, but will always argue that the net glamour-banality from it is positive. It might not be as great as a single work of art, but I think science always creates more wonder and more possibilities. I'll put it this way, I think magic(k) means all things thought of are possible, science means that things that haven't been thought of might be possible. I'm assuming the Technocracy doesn't exist here, just for the record.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm just na\u00efve though, and the internet wasn't created by scientists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Science can still create, which is great, but it limits things and rules possibilities out by definition. A new eureka can generate Glamour, but the plodding, repetitive methodology that gets there is often, ironically, very, very banal. That isn't a flaw in the setting--that's it's strength. The human and the fae, the Dreaming and the banal, the free and the organised are all things that need to exist. Imbalance is the real problem. </div> </div> </div>This is sort of what I'm asking for. The problem is that people say 'science=banal because technology', despite the fact that there's a lot of wonder in science. I don't think focusing on Science should be as profitable for changelings as 'creative' art forms, but I think they should be able to get Glamour from it at least semi-regularly. Why do we still tell stories about how great or terrible the world will be in the future.<br /> <br /> I may also be confusing less nuanced 'science is bad' works with Changeling, but then again I haven't actually been able to buy a corebook to give it a proper read.<br /> <br /> I will say that Maths is probably exempt from most of the 'science is banal' problems in my experience, but I don't know what the cutting edge of the field is like, so I may also be confused there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T09:09:13-08:00","id":781158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=781140#post781140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is sort of what I'm asking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should really need to read the nocker kithbook. You will find what you are looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T13:02:51-08:00","id":781281,"title":"","content":"this seems to be a major recurring argument with changeling fans. Does science = banality. Personally i think the truth would lie somewhere in the middle. It all depends on how the science is used. for example, the moon landing caused a huge surge of Glamour over the entire world, where as mass production and fast food are hot beds for banality. does the science involve creativity, wonder, and imagination? or does it make the world a duller place in general? Personally that's always what I thought would make science banal. After all, a Shakespearean play can be banal if it is uninspired, dull and utterly devoid of passion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T00:28:32-08:00","id":781596,"title":"","content":"I'd like Banality to not be seen as universally a bad thing. Humanity turned to Banality pretty whole sale for some reason. I'd like to see advantages to gaining banality rather than it as a punative measure for &quot;playing wrong&quot; Changelings should strive to bring balance to themselves and the two worlds not run away from either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:20:32-08:00","id":781876,"title":"","content":"There is also the fact that the science=banal thing might as well come from the general themes of WoD. Even if you don't believe in crossover, Werewolf and Mage portray science as static and banal. Though later editions have been better at portraying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T16:25:28-08:00","id":781927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=781876#post781876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the fact that the science=banal thing might as well come from the general themes of WoD. Even if you don't believe in crossover, Werewolf and Mage portray science as static and banal. Though later editions have been better at portraying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess the one reason I prefer Demon to Changeling. Guess.<br /> <br /> Yeah, science=bad really annoys me. I like how in Demon that at least some of the Fallen like that humanity has learnt to make and use complex tools. It's specifically the side effects of science that are bad, mainly pollution and possibly overuse of resources. If C20 makes science an explicit source of glamour but the scientific method banal, I think we'll all be happy.<br /> <br /> I know that science=static comes from a popular misconception of science, and don't fault the developers of the early editions for falling into it, especially as later editions cleared it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T21:54:47-08:00","id":782078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=781927#post781927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Guess the one reason I prefer Demon to Changeling. Guess.<br /> <br /> Yeah, science=bad really annoys me. I like how in Demon that at least some of the Fallen like that humanity has learnt to make and use complex tools. It's specifically the side effects of science that are bad, mainly pollution and possibly overuse of resources. If C20 makes science an explicit source of glamour but the scientific method banal, I think we'll all be happy.<br /> <br /> I know that science=static comes from a popular misconception of science, and don't fault the developers of the early editions for falling into it, especially as later editions cleared it up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Demon is also highly ambiguous about whether or not the approval of the Fallen is a good thing, considering the Source Material its referencing such as the Book of Enoch, I'd argue this is less saying something nice about science and more pointing out &quot;Hey Demons&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T00:33:23-08:00","id":782132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=782078#post782078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon is also highly ambiguous about whether or not the approval of the Fallen is a good thing, considering the Source Material its referencing such as the Book of Enoch, I'd argue this is less saying something nice about science and more pointing out &amp;quot;Hey Demons&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but at least Demons aren't 'science is bad'. They can be wrong and I'll still like the game, because of how they treat science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T01:57:50-08:00","id":782153,"title":"","content":"This is a setting of dark urban fantasy which is unscientific by nature. It's really not the end of the world if magic is therefore prioritised in the fluff over science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T02:07:28-08:00","id":782158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=782132#post782132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but at least Demons aren't 'science is bad'. They can be wrong and I'll still like the game, because of how they treat science.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you are misreading what I am saying. Demon can easily say &quot;Science is BAD&quot; as a game by having the Fallen say &quot;SCIENCE GOOD&quot; because its pretty clear in setting that the Fallen aren't exactly paragons of morality and self honesty. Demon like vampire pretty heavily relies on the probability that the majority of your type are in the wrong.<br /> <br /> MInd you that gets into my problem with Changeling because it doesn't hit on that, that the Dreaming is an unambigous good thing and that humanity embracing banality is an unambguous bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T11:48:47-08:00","id":782412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=782153#post782153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a setting of dark urban fantasy which is unscientific by nature. It's really not the end of the world if magic is therefore prioritised in the fluff over science.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I have no problem with. As long as the core C20 book doesn't say 'science always equals bad' I'm fine.<br /> <br /> Also, maybe I need to pick up come of the 2e books. Time to see if any relatives are still present shopping. The Nocker Kithbook is priority number 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=782158#post782158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are misreading what I am saying. Demon can easily say &quot;Science is BAD&quot; as a game by having the Fallen say &quot;SCIENCE GOOD&quot; because its pretty clear in setting that the Fallen aren't exactly paragons of morality and self honesty. Demon like vampire pretty heavily relies on the probability that the majority of your type are in the wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>To put it another way, different groups of demons have different views on science ranging from 'good but flawed' to 'meh'. I'm fine with the game saying 'demons are probably wrong', because the game doesn't side against science as the demons themselves aren't quite decided.<br /> <br /> {QUOTE]MInd you that gets into my problem with Changeling because it doesn't hit on that, that the Dreaming is an unambigous good thing and that humanity embracing banality is an unambguous bad thing. [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Yeah, I would like an upside to Banality to reduce this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T02:01:39-08:00","id":783300,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of issues I had with C:tD, but I don't know if they can be addressed without starting from scratch.<br /> <br /> 1. What are the themes and the antagonists? As tv tropes put it, &quot;It doesn't help that the game line itself has so many ways to go, you have little idea what the authors wanted\u2014a fable on the death of childhood innocence? A game of raging against the dying of the light? An urban fantasy game about balancing the fantastic and the mundane?&quot; Is it the lightest of the WoD games or the darkest? The core book has the primary struggle against Banality and it's agents, the Autumn People and the Dauntain. The trouble is that agents of Banality are by definition boring. So later books had the Shadow Court and the new Thallain as antagonists. The search for King David after being kidnapped by a Shadow Court member was introduced. Finally after the Week of Nightmares there were the Ahene and the Fomori Courts. Winter seemed to go from a general death of creativity, going out with a whimper, to a Garou style Apocalypse. Which of these will be in C20?<br /> <br /> 2. For a game emphasizing creativity, the players are limited to rigid, narrow Kiths. All trolls are honorable (blue) warriors, all pooka are liars, etc. There isn't even a &quot;none of the above&quot; option like Caitiff in Vampire or Orphans in Mage. They aren't really archetypal like the ones in DA: Fae and Lost, which led to Kith bloat. Again from tv tropes, &quot;Faerie races include the European Kithain (16, plus 8 Thallain), Native American Nunnehi (14), elemental Inanimae (6), Pacific Menehune (4), East Asian Hsien (10), Arabic Djinn (a fan work endorsed by the writers; 6), and the dark Adhene (7). There are over <i>70</i> different splats, not counting the potential for Australian, South American, Indian, and African fae (beyond the eshu) had the line been allowed to continue, which might have pushed that number towards 100. Each race has their own sets of rules, which keeps them separate from the others (plus geography).&quot; There's also 5 Inanimae and 13 Sidhe Houses. &quot;A word of warning for completists: because new splats could pop up seemingly at random, collecting all available <i>Dreaming</i> splats requires <i>15</i> books and a fan web supplement (a 1e or 2e corebook, <i>Immortal Eyes: The Toybox</i>, <i>Immortal Eyes: Shadows on the Hill</i>, <i>Immortal Eyes: Court of All Kings</i>, <i>Isle of the Mighty</i>, <i>The Fool's Luck</i>, <i>Kithbook: Redcaps</i>, <i>Kithbook: Eshu</i>, <i>World of Darkness: Blood-Dimmed Tides</i>, <i>The Shadow Court</i>, <i>Changeling Players Guide</i>, <i>Kingdom of Willows</i>, <i>Inanimae: The Secret Way</i>, <i>Land of Eight Million Dreams</i>, <i>Denizens of the Dreaming</i>, and web supplement <i>Djinn: Of Smokeless Fire</i>).&quot; Something with broad archetypes that could be customized, like DA: Fae and Lost mentioned above would be preferable, but then fans of the original Kiths would be left out.<br /> <br /> 3. The Eshu are problematic. They seem to be there to provide balance to the otherwise all European Kiths, but they're named after an African god, not actual African fae-like beings. They're also commoners, with the unfortunate implication that their natural rulers are the European Sidhe. Another book introduced the Oba as little known nobility of the Eshu, probably to fix this.<br /> <br /> 4. The Seelie/Unseelie dichotomy tends to turn into good vs. evil. Especially with the Thallain presented as really evil. It's presented as an innate characteristic, but only for the European Kiths. The Seasonal Court system or some other option would be preferable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T05:30:02-08:00","id":783388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=783300#post783300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. The Eshu are problematic. They seem to be there to provide balance to the otherwise all European Kiths, but they're named after an African god, not actual African fae-like beings. They're also commoners, with the unfortunate implication that their natural rulers are the European Sidhe. Another book introduced the Oba as little known nobility of the Eshu, probably to fix this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most of your points, but the impression I got of the Eshu was that they were nobles who didn't happen to care if other people realized it. Not quite sure where I picked that up as Changeling was a line I didn't read much, but I thought the Eshu and the Trolls were called out as displaced noble kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T12:21:30-08:00","id":783573,"title":"","content":"I'd like ....<br /> <br /> A) all previously published arts in the book. Corebook arts, Player's guide arts, Nobles SH arts, Fool's Luck arts, Shadow Court Arts, and the Merfolk arts too!<br /> <br /> B) I'd like a wide seclection of Kiths and the Native American, Hawaiian, and Chinese, Kiths, as well as the Inanimae and Adhene, in a Player Guide.<br /> <br /> C) I want both the Inanimae and the Hawaiian Fay fixed!<br /> <br /> D) I wan't their to be other kinds of third world kiths besides Eshu! (Mexico's Rain Dwarfs might be good, a few African Fays and Persian Peris)<br /> <br /> E) I want ways that participating in shared rituals can gather glamour for Changelings. It would make all their courts more logical and the festivals a lifeline.<br /> <br /> More later and revisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-10-2015, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T12:46:05-08:00","id":783589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=783573#post783573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like ....<br /> <br /> A) all previously published arts in the book. Corebook arts, Player's guide arts, Nobles SH arts, Fool's Luck arts, Shadow Court Arts, and the Merfolk arts too!<br /> <br /> B) I'd like a wide seclection of Kiths and the Native American, Hawaiian, and Chinese, Kiths, as well as the Inanimae and Adhene, in a Player Guide.<br /> <br /> C) I want both the Inanimae and the Hawaiian Fay fixed!<br /> <br /> D) I wan't their to be other kinds of third world kiths besides Eshu! (Mexico's Rain Dwarfs might be good, a few African Fays and Persian Peris)<br /> <br /> E) I want ways that participating in shared rituals can gather glamour for Changelings. It would make all their courts more logical and the festivals a lifeline.<br /> <br /> More later and revisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, on the other hand, want a book that won't kill a grown man on the street when dropped from a first floor window.<br /> <br /> I mean, those would be nice, but we have to be reasonable, putting in the Kiths and magic systems for a wide variety would probably mean we end up with nearing 1000 pages. I think the most we can reasonably expect is two types of Fae, the Shadow Court, and an appendix with the others in. On the other hand, I'd probably shell out for a supplementary book with everything you listed, I just don't believe it would fit in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T20:41:43-08:00","id":783902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=783388#post783388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with most of your points, but the impression I got of the Eshu was that they were nobles who didn't happen to care if other people realized it. Not quite sure where I picked that up as Changeling was a line I didn't read much, but I thought the Eshu and the Trolls were called out as displaced noble kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were some hints about Trolls, but not the Eshu, who were mostly regarded as vagabonds. That's why the aforementioned Oba were created as their nobility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T21:17:09-08:00","id":783914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=783589#post783589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I, on the other hand, want a book that won't kill a grown man on the street when dropped from a first floor window.<br /> <br /> I mean, those would be nice, but we have to be reasonable, putting in the Kiths and magic systems for a wide variety would probably mean we end up with nearing 1000 pages. I think the most we can reasonably expect is two types of Fae, the Shadow Court, and an appendix with the others in. On the other hand, I'd probably shell out for a supplementary book with everything you listed, I just don't believe it would fit in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's already met a stretch goal to add 10,000 words on how to create your very own kinds of Kiths, so page count creep is a possibility.<br /> <br /> Introducing flexibility like C:tL and DA:F is nice, but making it a stretch goal seems like an after thought. Will it only apply to the core book Kiths and not the Gallain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T21:33:30-08:00","id":783922,"title":"","content":"Stretch goals that add text to the physical book are not afterthoughts. Every page adds to the cost of writing, printing and shipping the books, which means some content won't make the cut for inclusion at the base funding level. When those stretch goals are hit, there's enough loose cash in the budget to roll into expanding the books with some of that cut content.<br /> <br /> Also, pretty sure any kiths you create will automatically count as Gallain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10165-flimflamberge","user":"Flimflamberge","date":".  second paragraph 12-11-2015, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10165-flimflamberge","name":"Flimflamberge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T23:11:57-08:00","id":783951,"title":"","content":"It wasn't even included in the initial stretch goals, so it doesn't seem to be a top priority. They might apply only to Kiths like the one in the core book with the Seelie/Unseelie split, which would make them a different kind of Kithain, not Gallain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T23:33:59-08:00","id":783956,"title":"","content":"Most stretch goals are planned way in advance of the Kickstarter. They only reveal them over time to prevent the negative connotations of putting them all up front. This was a very early one, which shows that it's definitely one they have firm plans for.<br /> <br /> Also, even the &quot;lesser kiths&quot; are considered Gallain. Piskies, clurichaun, ghille dhu, selkies and merfolk alike. Anything outside the nine major kiths is looked at as a weird cousin. Anyway, whatever guidelines there are should be very readily adaptable to Nunnehi, Adhene, Thallain, and even Inanimae if you think there's room for something new there. Only Hsien strike me as too divergent in splat structure, but like Inanimae their design implies there may not be any other types.<br /> <br /> (I can't speak to Menehune since Shadows on the Hill is one of the few books I never got my hands on. From what I understand they're no more different from Kithain than Nunnehi, though. Ditto for Dauntain with Autumn People. Do they even have splats?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10165-flimflamberge","name":"Flimflamberge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T02:26:14-08:00","id":784018,"title":"","content":"But it still wasn't included in the original draft, as opposed to things like the Hsien.<br /> <br /> There are no lesser Kiths, just rarer ones, and if it's a Kith it's not Gallain. From the Kickstarter:<ul><li>Rules for all of the kiths including in 2nd ed, plus fan favorites from other books: selkies, piskies, clurichaun, and both Arcadian and Concordian sidhe.</li> <li>Rules for the Gallain: The inanimae, the hsien, the Nunnehi, and others!</li> </ul><br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Kithain</b> is the name </a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Changeling_%28cWOD%29\" target=\"_blank\">Changelings</a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\"> use to describe themselves. Specifically, the Kithain are the </a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kith_%28cWOD%29\" target=\"_blank\">kith</a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\"> born of mortal dreams who possess both a </a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Seelie\" target=\"_blank\">Seelie</a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\"> and </a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Unseelie\" target=\"_blank\">Unseelie</a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Legacy_%28CTD%29\" target=\"_blank\">Legacy</a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\">. They include the </a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Sidhe\" target=\"_blank\">Sidhe</a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\"> and all the commoner kiths.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\">Other, non-Kithain fae include the </a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Thallain\" target=\"_blank\">Thallain</a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\"> (monstrous versions of the Kithain), the </a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Gallain?action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" target=\"_blank\">Gallain</a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\"> and the </a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Adhene\" target=\"_blank\">Adhene</a><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\">.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T02:29:23-08:00","id":784020,"title":"","content":"It was still not included in the original draft, unlike things such as the Hsien.<br /> <br /> There are no lesser Kiths, just rarer ones, and if it's a Kith it's not Gallain. From the Kickstarter,<ul><li>Rules for all of the kiths including in 2nd ed, plus fan favorites from other books: selkies, piskies, clurichaun, and both Arcadian and Concordian sidhe.</li> <li>Rules for the Gallain: The inanimae, the hsien, the Nunnehi, and others!</li> </ul><br /> From the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kithain\" target=\"_blank\">wiki</a>, &quot;<b>Kithain</b> is the name <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Changeling_%28cWOD%29\" target=\"_blank\">Changelings</a> use to describe themselves. Specifically, the Kithain are the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kith_%28cWOD%29\" target=\"_blank\">kith</a> born of mortal dreams who possess both a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Seelie\" target=\"_blank\">Seelie</a> and <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Unseelie\" target=\"_blank\">Unseelie</a> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Legacy_%28CTD%29\" target=\"_blank\">Legacy</a>. They include the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Sidhe\" target=\"_blank\">Sidhe</a> and all the commoner kiths.<br /> Other, non-Kithain fae include the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Thallain\" target=\"_blank\">Thallain</a> (monstrous versions of the Kithain), the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Gallain?veaction=edit&amp;redlink=1\" target=\"_blank\">Gallain</a> and the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Adhene\" target=\"_blank\">Adhene</a>.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","user":"Tau Neutrino","date":". 12-11-2015, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:38:31-08:00","id":784078,"title":"","content":"So wasn't the White Howler tribebook in W20, but it still affected the future books regardless.<br /> <br /> As for it not being included in the original draft, given the state of the book, there is plenty of time for it to affect the book still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T06:01:54-08:00","id":784100,"title":"","content":"Word counts are a thing. Some things might be cool to have, but you've got to pick what's necessary vs what would be nice.<br /> <br /> In one of my sections there was some stuff I thought would be fun to include, but I quickly realized I just didn't have the space. I didn't even start writing the things I knew I wouldn't be able to fit, and I still ended up about 4000 words over my assigned word count. I had to cut it down before I submitted my draft.<br /> <br /> These sorts of things aren't after thoughts. They're just the reality of constrained space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T06:23:35-08:00","id":784115,"title":"","content":"Lordy, the things I would have done if not constrained by word count... One of my drafts went in 1000 words over count, and that was after paring another 2000 words out of it. <br /> <br /> Trust me, we're all feeling the &quot;man, wouldn't it be cool if I had another 5-10k to play with?&quot; But the book is huge, and you gotta be choosy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T12:45:51-08:00","id":784298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=783589#post783589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I, on the other hand, want a book that won't kill a grown man on the street when dropped from a first floor window.<br /> <br /> I mean, those would be nice, but we have to be reasonable, putting in the Kiths and magic systems for a wide variety would probably mean we end up with nearing 1000 pages. I think the most we can reasonably expect is two types of Fae, the Shadow Court, and an appendix with the others in. On the other hand, I'd probably shell out for a supplementary book with everything you listed, I just don't believe it would fit in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did want several types of Kiths in a player's Guide. If the Corebook had the standard Kith's and a players guide had the Adhene, the Native American Fay, the Hawaiian Fay, the East Asian fay, the Merfolk, the Inanimae, and some Third-world Kiths, like Mexican Rain Dwarfs, Peri, ect. would six to nine extra kiths in the corebook wound you too deeply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-12-2015, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T15:10:11-08:00","id":784371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=783573#post783573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like ....<br /> <br /> A) all previously published arts in the book. Corebook arts, Player's guide arts, Nobles SH arts, Fool's Luck arts, Shadow Court Arts, and the Merfolk arts too!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arts are a balance of two competing goals:<br /> <br /> 1) Bring back everything cool!<br /> <br /> 2) Ensure that it is actually cool.<br /> <br /> A lot of the old Arts, we discovered, were like... not actually cool. Nobles: the Shining Host had an Art that did basically nothing but alleviate optional penalties that an optional sub-system introduced into that book tossed onto the sidhe, and which no subsequent book ever referenced again, and which I've never heard of anyone actually using in play. So that didn't seem like a great thing to bring back. Then there was the Art in the Shadow Court which did nothing but go &quot;nuh-uh&quot; to various dots of Sovereign, which is a worst-of-all-worlds combination of expensive, boring, and really limited. Like, you just sit around waiting for the Duke to use Sovereign on you and then hope you have the right dot to shut him down? Why make that a whole <i>Art?</i> Why not just one dot of an Art to let you throw off oaths or bonds of authority, if you gotta have a power like that in the first place, and then give you proactive things with the other dots?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Changeling's core array of Arts were always very <i>small and limited</i> in the past, with a lot of things the fiction implied they ought to be able to do not actually falling within the scope of any published Art. (Remember how the books used to imply the Sluagh would hang around gossiping with ghosts, but then there was absolutely nothing except maybe a Merit somewhere that would have enabled that?) Like, Chicanery, Wayfare, Primal, they were great, but there were only, what, 7 powers in the corebook? Gotta have more than that to play with.<br /> <br /> So what C20 has is a best-of compilation and reworking of the Arts. We looked at every dot of every old Art from allllll the supplements and decided what to do with each. Some of the very limited Arts of old got crunched down to their best one or two powers and folded into another Art. Other Arts got moderate to major power bumps. Others still-- particularly the &quot;Kith-specific&quot; ones-- became core sub-systems. EVERY Art got its dot progression reviewed and overhauled for better consistency, <i>and</i> to ensure that all dots of all Arts were compatible with all Realms-- no more ersatz Disciplines that ignore the Realms system, making all of your Arts much more versatile than in the past. And of course there are several completely new Arts, to boot.<br /> <br /> No Arts were cut from the current draft for space, to be clear-- all changes were made for better versatility, bang-for-your-buck, and playability. If an old Art isn't there in stand-alone form like it used to be, you will probably find its best features folded into one of the old Arts or cobbled into one of the new Arts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T15:27:59-08:00","id":784383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=784371#post784371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Arts are a balance of two competing goals:<br /> <br /> 1) Bring back everything cool!<br /> <br /> 2) Ensure that it is actually cool.<br /> <br /> A lot of the old Arts, we discovered, were like... not actually cool. Nobles: the Shining Host had an Art that did basically nothing but alleviate optional penalties that an optional sub-system introduced into that book tossed onto the sidhe, and which no subsequent book ever referenced again, and which I've never heard of anyone actually using in play. So that didn't seem like a great thing to bring back. Then there was the Art in the Shadow Court which did nothing but go &amp;quot;nuh-uh&amp;quot; to various dots of Sovereign, which is a worst-of-all-worlds combination of expensive, boring, and really limited. Like, you just sit around waiting for the Duke to use Sovereign on you and then hope you have the right dot to shut him down? Why make that a whole <i>Art?</i> Why not just one dot of an Art to let you throw off oaths or bonds of authority, if you gotta have a power like that in the first place, and then give you proactive things with the other dots?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Changeling's core array of Arts were always very <i>small and limited</i> in the past, with a lot of things the fiction implied they ought to be able to do not actually falling within the scope of any published Art. (Remember how the books used to imply the Sluagh would hang around gossiping with ghosts, but then there was absolutely nothing except maybe a Merit somewhere that would have enabled that?) Like, Chicanery, Wayfare, Primal, they were great, but there were only, what, 7 powers in the corebook? Gotta have more than that to play with.<br /> <br /> So what C20 has is a best-of compilation and reworking of the Arts. We looked at every dot of every old Art from allllll the supplements and decided what to do with each. Some of the very limited Arts of old got crunched down to their best one or two powers and folded into another Art. Other Arts got moderate to major power bumps. Others still-- particularly the &amp;quot;Kith-specific&amp;quot; ones-- became core sub-systems. EVERY Art got its dot progression reviewed and overhauled for better consistency, <i>and</i> to ensure that all dots of all Arts were compatible with all Realms-- no more ersatz Disciplines that ignore the Realms system, making all of your Arts much more versatile than in the past. And of course there are several completely new Arts, to boot.<br /> <br /> No Arts were cut from the current draft for space, to be clear-- all changes were made for better versatility, bang-for-your-buck, and playability. If an old Art isn't there in stand-alone form like it used to be, you will probably find its best features folded into one of the old Arts or cobbled into one of the new Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't wait to see this chapter. Can we backers have this as our first sneak peek, please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T15:52:17-08:00","id":784392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=784298#post784298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did want several types of Kiths in a player's Guide. If the Corebook had the standard Kith's and a players guide had the Adhene, the Native American Fay, the Hawaiian Fay, the East Asian fay, the Merflok, the Inanimae, and some Third-world Kiths, like Mexican Rain Dwarfs, Peri, ect. would six to nine extra kiths in the corebook wound you too deeply?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll put it this way: new kiths will take up about two pages. As long as they don't go overboard I wouldn't mind every fan favourite kith being put in, provided they don't have to add any special 'just for them' magics. In short, I'm fine as long as new kiths only add things to the kiths section.<br /> <br /> Now, if there's a type of fae people really want and has significant changes to the magic system, I'm fine with that, as long as it's an appendix like V20's bloodlines and W20's kinfolk and changing breeds (I really want W20, to the point where it's the one game where I just flat out won't buy anything I see until I get the 20th anniversary edition). I feel like C20 should be accessible to those like me who have never played before and so want a campaign with only the 'basic' kiths and magics.<br /> <br /> On the reworking of the arts, versatile ones sound wonderful. I really want this book to be out as soon as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T16:10:18-08:00","id":784395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=782412#post782412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This I have no problem with. As long as the core C20 book doesn't say 'science always equals bad' I'm fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal take has always been that banality isn't necessarily a job or a field of study; it's more often a state of mind or a lifestyle. It's all in how you approach what you're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T17:07:18-08:00","id":784418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=784392#post784392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the reworking of the arts, versatile ones sound wonderful. I really want this book to be out as soon as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Arts/Realms system is an amazing thing that very few old Changeling supplements really engaged in any depth. It really rewards creative use. I mean, sure, there's the obvious use of Wayfare \u2022, Hopscotch, make yourself jump really well. And that's great. But slap on Prop \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and aim it at the car full of baddies chasing you down the freeway, and all of a sudden you have something terrifyingly formidable on your hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T17:14:18-08:00","id":784421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=784418#post784418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Me too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Arts/Realms system is an amazing thing that very few old Changeling supplements really engaged in any depth. It really rewards creative use. I mean, sure, there's the obvious use of Wayfare \u2022, Hopscotch, make yourself jump really well. And that's great. But slap on Prop \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and aim it at the car full of baddies chasing you down the freeway, and all of a sudden you have something terrifyingly formidable on your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus the suggestion that you might use it to siphon ('jump') Glamour from one being to another with Fae 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T20:52:22-08:00","id":785728,"title":"","content":"I think we can agree that word count limitations are Banal. <br /> <br /> As to doing science, it's more jumping through hoops to get funding and tenure taking away from doing your research that's Banal IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T21:42:39-08:00","id":785748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=784115#post784115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lordy, the things I would have done if not constrained by word count... One of my drafts went in 1000 words over count, and that was after paring another 2000 words out of it.<br /> <br /> Trust me, we're all feeling the &quot;man, wouldn't it be cool if I had another 5-10k to play with?&quot; But the book is huge, and you gotta be choosy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could always be like Mage and make the game 650 page and then 3 books of &quot;I wanted really add this but 1k books aren't happening&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T21:48:52-08:00","id":785754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=784418#post784418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Me too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Arts/Realms system is an amazing thing that very few old Changeling supplements really engaged in any depth. It really rewards creative use. I mean, sure, there's the obvious use of Wayfare \u2022, Hopscotch, make yourself jump really well. And that's great. But slap on Prop \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and aim it at the car full of baddies chasing you down the freeway, and all of a sudden you have something terrifyingly formidable on your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sovereign and prop was always the fun one for us &quot;I COMMAND THIS CAR TO OPEN!&quot; &quot;Weapons shall not piece my glory!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T08:16:14-08:00","id":785986,"title":"","content":"I really like what I read in Holden's post about what they did to recombine and beef up Arts. I especially like the notion of kith-specific Arts becoming subsystems in their own rights; subsystems, in my experience with gaming, tend to be the things that get MOST engaged with and which are most able to express mechanically an interesting aspect of the setting. I hope what they're planning with Realms will be equally more engaging, rather than having them serve as clunky gatekeepers to being able to actually USE your Arts.<br /> <br /> (I understand some of that will be necessary, but I always felt like Changeling's Realms were more limits than allowances. &quot;No, you CAN'T use your Hopscotch ability because you don't have 3 dots in two different Realms!&quot; This may be an exaggeration with Hopscotch, but there were Arts that felt like they had certain Realms required at high ranking before they could at all be useful. And I confess that I'm not sure the Fae Realm was a good one at all. It was pure barring of use, rather than permissive use.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T06:31:02-08:00","id":786686,"title":"","content":"I can tell you that Holden's and Jonathan's Arts &amp; Realms chapter is all kinds of awesome in my book. Not that it's passed unnoticed since Holden posted here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T07:01:01-08:00","id":786698,"title":"","content":"Frankly, as great as the revisions to the Arts sound, what got my attention was the addition of Unleashing. If it's anything like the Unleashing from <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b>, then C20 will be in a position to rival <b>Mage</b> in terms of power and versatility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T07:07:49-08:00","id":786701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=784418#post784418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Me too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Arts/Realms system is an amazing thing that very few old Changeling supplements really engaged in any depth. It really rewards creative use. I mean, sure, there's the obvious use of Wayfare \u2022, Hopscotch, make yourself jump really well. And that's great. But slap on Prop \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and aim it at the car full of baddies chasing you down the freeway, and all of a sudden you have something terrifyingly formidable on your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://youtu.be/LUlhkgffLtQ?t=205\" target=\"_blank\">QUALITY car chases</a>, explained through Changeling!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:09:01-08:00","id":793718,"title":"","content":"Following on from this, which house rules that you've implemented would you like to see in C20?<br /> <br /> Following on from a debate I read recently on RPG.net, I'd like either an easier way to Musing or an alternative way of harvesting Glamour that's more akin to hunting in VTM. <br /> <br /> Mages and wraiths get to meditate for instance, but changelings have to inspire art. Why not just let changelings spend some time engaged in their own creative pursuits and allow a roll at the end to restore Glamour? First drafts and aborted works are still creative, and are absolutely necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:59:49-08:00","id":793747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=793718#post793718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following on from this, which house rules that you've implemented would you like to see in C20?<br /> <br /> Following on from a debate I read recently on RPG.net, I'd like either an easier way to Musing or an alternative way of harvesting Glamour that's more akin to hunting in VTM.<br /> <br /> Mages and wraiths get to meditate for instance, but changelings have to inspire art. Why not just let changelings spend some time engaged in their own creative pursuits and allow a roll at the end to restore Glamour? First drafts and aborted works are still creative, and are absolutely necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>How'd that be different from Rapture? 'Cause Rapture is exactly that - regaining Glamour from your own creativity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T13:29:45-08:00","id":793762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=793718#post793718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following on from this, which house rules that you've implemented would you like to see in C20?<br /> <br /> Following on from a debate I read recently on RPG.net, I'd like either an easier way to Musing or an alternative way of harvesting Glamour that's more akin to hunting in VTM.<br /> <br /> Mages and wraiths get to meditate for instance, but changelings have to inspire art. Why not just let changelings spend some time engaged in their own creative pursuits and allow a roll at the end to restore Glamour? First drafts and aborted works are still creative, and are absolutely necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've been thinking about this. Mages have a background called &quot;Legend&quot; where you get quintessence by following what the Technocracy calls &quot;The Hyper narrative&quot; this seems even more approrpriate for Changelings, so I was thinking that might be the &quot;feeding&quot; equivalent. When you go out and live the life of proper knight! Or when you tell your enemies your elaborate plan before finishing them off in this easily escaped death trap, living as creatures of the Dream and bringing the Dream to life should spread glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T04:41:22-08:00","id":794094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=793762#post793762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I've been thinking about this. Mages have a background called &quot;Legend&quot; where you get quintessence by following what the Technocracy calls &quot;The Hyper narrative&quot; this seems even more approrpriate for Changelings, so I was thinking that might be the &quot;feeding&quot; equivalent. When you go out and live the life of proper knight! Or when you tell your enemies your elaborate plan before finishing them off in this easily escaped death trap, living as creatures of the Dream and bringing the Dream to life should spread glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a great idea. I had a similar idea, but tied to Legacies instead. However, perhaps these could be tied into kiths? So that each kith has a legend which will generate Glamour for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-28-2015, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T10:06:07-08:00","id":794240,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd like to see the flaw Echoes transformed into a inherent mechanic. Changelings can <u>choose</u> to follow certain &quot;faerie strictures&quot; which are inconvenient. Following them gains glamour when it inconveniences them to do so; breaking them can gain banality if they're under a certain level of it.<br /> <br /> And the trouble with Rapture is that, like Musing, it takes weeks to months (because it has to be &quot;real art&quot; and that obviously can't be done in just a few hours), and returns pittances of Glamour. Changelings have tiny &quot;magic mojo&quot; pools, and expend them fast if they want to do anything, and take at least several days (and more likely longer than a week or more) to get any back. This needs to change. The inflow has to be more reasonable, or the outflow far rarer (perhaps spending Glamour is something that is only needed for &quot;extra oomph,&quot; the way a lot of Quintessence expenditure is for Mages).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T11:05:48-08:00","id":794280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=794240#post794240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd like to see the flaw Echoes transformed into a inherent mechanic. Changelings can <u>choose</u> to follow certain &amp;quot;faerie strictures&amp;quot; which are inconvenient. Following them gains glamour when it inconveniences them to do so; breaking them can gain banality if they're under a certain level of it.<br /> <br /> And the trouble with Rapture is that, like Musing, it takes weeks to months (because it has to be &amp;quot;real art&amp;quot; and that obviously can't be done in just a few hours), and returns pittances of Glamour. Changelings have tiny &amp;quot;magic mojo&amp;quot; pools, and expend them fast if they want to do anything, and take at least several days (and more likely longer than a week or more) to get any back. This needs to change. The inflow has to be more reasonable, or the outflow far rarer (perhaps spending Glamour is something that is only needed for &amp;quot;extra oomph,&amp;quot; the way a lot of Quintessence expenditure is for Mages).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Matt implied that Birthrights will mostly be free to use now, instead of costing Glamour. Which helps a little. But yeah, I like your Echoes idea as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:17:56-08:00","id":794316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=794240#post794240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd like to see the flaw Echoes transformed into a inherent mechanic. Changelings can <u>choose</u> to follow certain &quot;faerie strictures&quot; which are inconvenient. Following them gains glamour when it inconveniences them to do so; breaking them can gain banality if they're under a certain level of it.<br /> <br /> And the trouble with Rapture is that, like Musing, it takes weeks to months (because it has to be &quot;real art&quot; and that obviously can't be done in just a few hours), and returns pittances of Glamour. Changelings have tiny &quot;magic mojo&quot; pools, and expend them fast if they want to do anything, and take at least several days (and more likely longer than a week or more) to get any back. This needs to change. The inflow has to be more reasonable, or the outflow far rarer (perhaps spending Glamour is something that is only needed for &quot;extra oomph,&quot; the way a lot of Quintessence expenditure is for Mages).</div> </div> </div> </div>And this here is why stuff like the Accordance War never made sense to me. Along with Banality being so bad, it made no sense for there to be enough glamour even then to truly war with one another in sieges and castles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T15:13:01-08:00","id":794413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=794240#post794240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd like to see the flaw Echoes transformed into a inherent mechanic. Changelings can <u>choose</u> to follow certain &quot;faerie strictures&quot; which are inconvenient. Following them gains glamour when it inconveniences them to do so; breaking them can gain banality if they're under a certain level of it.<br /> <br /> And the trouble with Rapture is that, like Musing, it takes weeks to months (because it has to be &quot;real art&quot; and that obviously can't be done in just a few hours), and returns pittances of Glamour. Changelings have tiny &quot;magic mojo&quot; pools, and expend them fast if they want to do anything, and take at least several days (and more likely longer than a week or more) to get any back. This needs to change. The inflow has to be more reasonable, or the outflow far rarer (perhaps spending Glamour is something that is only needed for &quot;extra oomph,&quot; the way a lot of Quintessence expenditure is for Mages).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like echos, though I kind of like the idea of &quot;changeling is really big into star wars and tries to tap into its glamour&quot;<br /> <br /> As for Musing and Rapture, you hit that on the head, the fiction treated them as so much greater than they were, but dross and freeholds were mechanically the only real method of doing much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T17:38:25-08:00","id":794494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=794413#post794413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like echos, though I kind of like the idea of &amp;quot;changeling is really big into star wars and tries to tap into its glamour&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> As for Musing and Rapture, you hit that on the head, the fiction treated them as so much greater than they were, but dross and freeholds were mechanically the only real method of doing much.</div> </div> </div> </div>The system also fails to take into account process, I think, and focuses too much on outcomes. A changeling should be able to regain Glamour from all those breakthroughs, epiphanies and eureka moments throughout the process of creating, rather than just the finished product.<br /> <br /> Even when an artist doesn't create anything new, process can be a truly rewarding experience which fires up the imagination and teaches the artist invaluable lessons. This should generate Glamour.<br /> <br /> The amount of Glamour should be higher too. A poem should generate 10 or more points of Glamour. A novel should generate 20, 50, maybe even more...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T17:54:50-08:00","id":794504,"title":"","content":"The as-presented Musing and Rapture would work if they gave huge rewards and Changelings had huge (or cap-less) Glamour pools. That is, they could accumulate huge amounts, which then could be depleted over time while they get no new infusions for a long while. And then they get another big one from the next work of art they inspire or create.<br /> <br /> Heck, you could keep the cap in place and have it apply to what you can get from a Freehold's balefire and the like.<br /> <br /> Dross was, sadly, never developed enough for me to know how to use it in the core rules, and I don't have any of the expansions. I cannot therefore comment on it without a lot of speculation. It <u>sounds</u> like you can have an unlimited amount of Glamour if you keep art kitsch with you all the time, and are willing to destroy it. But that seems...weird, to me, from a &quot;how the myths work&quot; standpoint. Draining it should make it lose some &quot;significance,&quot; not be physically ruined. At least, not necessarily be physically ruined. Using it as a tool in your bunk and having that use destroy it is one thing. Pulling something out of it for use as a magical thing that vanishes, but leaves your art work bereft of its elements, could work. But it should also be possible to just realize that this great work of art is actually nothing special; people just built up this &quot;Picasso&quot; fellow to unrealistic levels when you look at the work that surely was just his students' scribblings to which he signed his name. (In reality, they once WERE the grand works of art that they're known for being...but have had the Glamour drained as dross, leaving them over-hyped junk pieces now.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T18:34:34-08:00","id":794525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/777632-what-this-humble-changeling-fan-wishes-for-the-c20-edition?p=794504#post794504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The as-presented Musing and Rapture would work if they gave huge rewards and Changelings had huge (or cap-less) Glamour pools. That is, they could accumulate huge amounts, which then could be depleted over time while they get no new infusions for a long while. And then they get another big one from the next work of art they inspire or create.<br /> <br /> Heck, you could keep the cap in place and have it apply to what you can get from a Freehold's balefire and the like.<br /> <br /> Dross was, sadly, never developed enough for me to know how to use it in the core rules, and I don't have any of the expansions. I cannot therefore comment on it without a lot of speculation. It <u>sounds</u> like you can have an unlimited amount of Glamour if you keep art kitsch with you all the time, and are willing to destroy it. But that seems...weird, to me, from a &quot;how the myths work&quot; standpoint. Draining it should make it lose some &quot;significance,&quot; not be physically ruined. At least, not necessarily be physically ruined. Using it as a tool in your bunk and having that use destroy it is one thing. Pulling something out of it for use as a magical thing that vanishes, but leaves your art work bereft of its elements, could work. But it should also be possible to just realize that this great work of art is actually nothing special; people just built up this &quot;Picasso&quot; fellow to unrealistic levels when you look at the work that surely was just his students' scribblings to which he signed his name. (In reality, they once WERE the grand works of art that they're known for being...but have had the Glamour drained as dross, leaving them over-hyped junk pieces now.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mementos are rarely destroyed for Glamour. More likely, changelings will use dross in uncrafted forms: toadstools, stones, moss, etc. Destroying mementos (artworks-as-dross) is generally frowned upon.<br /> <br /> The large amounts of Glamour I've suggested above should probably be given out gradually (over a month for a short story, over a year for a novel). That way, they can slowly provide Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}